    "objective": "Construct canonical layer L07 Trade-off Mitigation (StageId.MITIGATION) as a real, gate-routed stage of the autonomous SoftLoop, executing between L06 TRADEOFF and L08 DESIGN.\n\n=== 0. STATUS OF THIS DOCUMENT ===\nThis is the L06 TRADEOFF synthesis. It supersedes the pre-synthesis intake of the same goal_signature. Inputs synthesized: DERIV-L07 (L03 re-derivation, RC-1..RC-12, U1-U8, BL-1..BL-6), the L04 IdeationSet (candidates A/B/C/D, CC-1..CC-5, OPEN-VERIFY-1..5), and the L05 ResearchDossier (blocker resolutions, findings F-N1..F-N9, constraint register R-*, revised acceptance test). Where those three disagree, this document decides, and says why.\n\n=== 1. WHY THIS TARGET (unchanged, and now verified) ===\nL07 is the first FULLY-MISSING layer in the canonical chain. Both neighbours (L06 TRADEOFF, L08 DESIGN) are built and orchestrated, so it depends on no missing layer. It repairs the earliest illegal edge in the live walk and closes a constitutional violation present on EVERY historical run: operations/ENGINEERING_LIFECYCLE.md:116 makes L08 entry conditional on L07 mitigations, and L08 has never received them.\nTwo premises of that rationale were challenged upstream and are now resolved:\n- BL-1 / RC-12 (blocking): the claim that 'zero kernel/ edits' does not imply SOFT is FALSIFIED. constitution/classifier_rules/ is empty but the classifier does not read it (reviews/tasks/B0.11_review.md:39, 'No regex, no config'); the rule is top-path-segment in {kernel, constitution} => HARD, else SOFT. The change set below has no such segment and classifies SOFT, corroborated by ~15 recorded F2-SOFT classifications on these exact paths (B1.C_review.md:13, B1-SOFTLOOP_review.md:13, B2.O_review.md, phase3-scheduler_review.md). The prior HARD labels on DEBT-0001/0002 were produced over the run's implicated-paths set (which contains the bare directory 'kernel/'), not over a change set. The 'only candidate the current self-hosting loop can seal' premise holds.