ked by a normative ordering contradiction no table can resolve: spec/PAEOS-7:367 and the StageId numbering put RE_DERIVE BEFORE INTAKE, while operations/ENGINEERING_LIFECYCLE.md:49-71 (FROZEN v1.0) and spec/PAEOS-9:723-725 put re-derivation AFTER triage. C's generality is therefore banked later than L04 assumed and F-C3 (premature abstraction) is likelier than L04 scored it. C is successor goal #2, gated behind that resolution.\n\n=== 3. BINDING IMPLEMENTATION CONSTRAINTS ===\nBC-1. Insert StageId.MITIGATION into the SoftLoop._run_body stage sequence BETWEEN TRADEOFF and DESIGN. Not appended, not parallel. Key the insertion on StageId IDENTITY ('after TRADEOFF, before DESIGN'), NEVER on an integer slot - the corpus carries four incompatible stage numberings (R-KEY / RC-10).\nBC-2. Add a _MITIGATION RoleSpec and its ROLE_SPECS entry in runtime/agents/__init__.py. Role PLANNER. Runtime write scope for the stage agent: 'mitigation/' ONLY. Copy the _DESIGN precedent (design/, plan/, enforced by the dispatcher with ScopeViolation); NEVER copy the _EVOLVE precedent (write_scopes=('runtime/','kernel/') on a PLANNER role, which is a planner authorised to write TCB). Do not grant the stage agent runtime/, kernel/, or ledger/. This is the L07 agent's run-time scope, distinct from this intake's builder scopes.\nBC-2a. _MITIGATION.mcp_servers MUST include 'court' and 'artifacts'. This is the single highest-value item and it is checked FIRST (see PC-1): L07 is a PLANNER stage that must submit evidence, and that combination has never been exercised. The path does not need Bash - the CAS put returns the hash (spec/PAEOS-7.6:237-238), court.submit_evidence is an MCP method, and the KERNEL re-runs the reproducible_command (T2), not the agent. The tested live path is worker -> submit_evidence MCP -> FileCourtEvidencePool -> McpWorkerTransport as an EvidenceSource -> seal (reviews/tasks/R5.3_review.md).\nBC-3. Bind a NON-EMPTY required_evidence obligation. It is TWO obligations, not one:\n   (i) a DETERMINISTIC coverage check (kind TEST or PROOF, determinism DETERMINISTIC) whose reproducible_command loads the L06 matrix and the L07 catalogue BY CAS HASH and asserts totality of the mapping {rows at or above HIGH under AMENDMENT-1} -> {named safeguard} union {accepted-risk record}. This is the obligation that can actually deny, and the kernel re-runs it.\n   (ii) a CITATION obligation binding the catalogue to the L06 matrix's artifact_hash (SI-4 stale-replay defence).\nFollow the _RE_DERIVE / _IDEATE precedent for NON-EMPTINESS. Do not read that precedent as mandating CITATION alone; a judgment-only obligation makes L07's exit unfalsifiable by the kernel, which is CANARY-0002 with extra steps. Do NOT extend the required_evidence=() drift shipped in _RESEARCH / _CRITIQUE / _TRADEOFF (that drift is an incident to surface, not to fix here).\nBC-4. Emit a real mitigation catalogue artifact (kill switches, fallback behaviour, shadow mode, safety constraints) to the CAS and carry it to DESIGN over the existing planner_artifacts chain, so L08's entry condition is met in fact. artifact_hash MUST reference the CAS entry, never a filesystem path digest. 'mitigation/' is a working scope, not the artifact's address.\nBC-4a. THE EMPTY CATALOGUE IS A FIRST-CLASS CASE, not an error path. operations/WORKFLOW_STATE_MACHINE.yaml:180 offers L06 a 'no material risk' exit straight to L08; the kernel lattice does not permit it, so every substantial run enters L07 including runs with a clean matrix, and must emit a well-formed EMPTY catalogue with a bound hash. The oracle must accept a well-formed empty catalogue while rejecting a MISSING one. A design that only handles 'there are risks' deadlocks every goal with a clean L06 matrix.\nBC-5. Route BOTH MITIGATION edges through Gate.propose_transition with the four-tuple, binding the catalogue hash as evidence. Mint and RECORD a gate_id (G-Mitigate is the obvious form): ValidationClaim.gate_id is a required field and the r