O direct TRADEOFF -> DESIGN edge. Explicitly NOT asserted on the ROUTINE compression path: ROUTINE may legally take TRIAGE -> IMPLEMENT, where MITIGATION is never entered and there is no four-tuple; an unqualified assertion reports a false failure there.\nD2. ARTIFACT. The MITIGATION stage emits a catalogue to the CAS and the transition's evidence carries an artifact_hash equal to that CAS hash - INCLUDING on a clean matrix, where the catalogue is a well-formed EMPTY catalogue and not a missing one (BC-4a).\nD3. THE GATE CAN DENY, AND DENIES FOR THE RIGHT REASON. With the obligation unmet, the transition REMANDs AND the court evidence pool is non-empty AND contains the coverage-check evidence with a false result. A test asserting only outcome != COMMITTED DOES NOT DISCHARGE THIS CRITERION - it cannot distinguish a working gate from a broken submission path. The discriminator is the pool itself, already used in anger once (empty pool => submission path broken => test invalid, retry; pool carries the failing coverage evidence => the obligation genuinely discriminated).\nD4. NON-VACUITY, MECHANICALLY. The coverage check is run through a vacuous_commands-style with/without comparison and shown to discriminate. repo_root MUST be set or the check is skipped and proves nothing.\nD5. TRACE-A. A ROUTINE goal walking the full chain transitions TRADEOFF -> MITIGATION -> DESIGN with an {auto_pass, trace_a, runtime} evidence stub BOUND to a real CAS catalogue object. Auto-discharge is not skip, and a stub with nothing to bind to fails SI-4 (evidence whose artifact_hash is not the artifact under review is rejected). If no live weight class currently reaches this path, test it at unit level - do not drop it.\nPROCESS CRITERION:\nD6. A reviews/tasks/ constitutional implementation review exists for the increment (BC-8).\n\n=== 6. DEBT AND INCIDENTS ===\nCER-3 DEBT TO RECORD WITH THIS INCREMENT, each with an explicit repayment condition:\n- Deferred adversary, if PC-3 does not clear.